%S A401803 1,1,6,118,6175,790251,237322652,163186832348,252604882858797,
%T A401803 869071225495132105,6578287759822466474050,
%U A401803 108641406196141858066341810,3887513944470951468646971461723,299615185208345424463833037048709015,49482209477008382329022645745978677821560
%N A401803 Number of equivalence classes under column permutations of (n+1) X n binary matrices with at least two 1's in each column and an n X n submatrix with permanent 1.
%C A401803 The rows are labeled; only columns may be permuted. The columns are necessarily distinct.
%C A401803 Equivalently, a(n) counts n-element families F of distinct subsets of {1,...,n+1}, each containing at least two elements, such that, for at least one element x, there is exactly one way to choose a representative from each member of F, with all representatives distinct and none equal to x.
%C A401803 Each family is counted once, even if several choices of x satisfy this condition.
%H A401803 Vaclav Kotesovec, <a href="/A401803/b401803.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..76</a>
%F A401803 a(0) = a(1) = 1. For n >= 2, a(n) = Sum_{k=1..n} (-1)^(k+1) * binomial(n+1,k) * (2^(n-k+1)-1)^k * a(n-k).
%F A401803 a(n) ~ c * n! * n * 2^(n*(n+1)/2) / A245654^n, where c = 0.24353526977294780998453606344321756236030486311... - _Vaclav Kotesovec_, Nov 06 2026
%e A401803 For n = 5, the family F = {{1,2,3,4,5,6}, {2,3,4,5,6}, {3,4,5,6}, {4,5,6}, {5,6}} is counted: every member has at least two elements, and excluding 6 forces the representatives, in reverse order, to be 5, 4, 3, 2, 1.
%t A401803 a[n_] := a[n] = If[n < 2, 1, Sum[(-1)^(k+1) * Binomial[n+1, k] * (2^(n-k+1) - 1)^k * a[n-k], {k, 1, n}]]; Table[a[n], {n, 0, 15}] (* _Vaclav Kotesovec_, Nov 06 2026 *)
%Y A401803 Cf. A400648 (without the restriction on column sums), A342598, A342599.
%Y A401803 Cf. A188455, A245654.
